# Back controls

Do not write “← Toronto farmers' markets” or any destination-labelled back crumb. That reads as generated.

Primary pages (Events, Markets, Feed, Saved) have no back link. The header wordmark and nav are how you leave.

Nested pages (a market, a stall) use `BackButton`: round hit target, `CaretLeftMark`, `aria-label="Back"`, no visible label. Same-origin referrer calls `router.back()`; otherwise go to the parent index.

```tsx
// BAD
<Link href="/">← Toronto farmers' markets</Link>

// GOOD — nested page only
<BackButton href="/markets" />
```
